    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Recurrent episodes of fever with shaking chills and drenching sweats, three in the past two years, each beginning months after naval service in malaria-endemic areas; the first diagnosed as malaria abroad on a blood smear with the species not recorded and treated with chloroquine alone, the later two treated with chloroquine without testing; the last ended six weeks before intake; afebrile and well at intake; cause not established at intake; infectious diseases consultation requested</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R50.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented recurrent attacks of illness called malaria; superseded by the diagnosis at the infectious diseases consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Pre-travel care for a naval deployment, expected to sail early next year, to French Guiana and the French Antilles: yellow fever vaccination required for entry to French Guiana, malaria prevention, dengue, chikungunya and typhus prevention by vector avoidance, food and water safety, and travel vaccines</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z71.84</td><td>S — Synthetic modern counterpart of his documented preparation of a tropical campaign in 1705.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

