<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Recurrent episodes of fever with shaking chills and drenching sweats, three in the past two years, each beginning months after naval service in malaria-endemic areas; the first diagnosed as malaria abroad on a blood smear with the species not recorded and treated with chloroquine alone, the later two treated with chloroquine without testing; the last ended six weeks before intake; afebrile and well at intake; cause not established at intake; infectious diseases consultation requested: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Pre-travel care for a naval deployment, expected to sail early next year, to French Guiana and the French Antilles: yellow fever vaccination required for entry to French Guiana, malaria prevention, dengue, chikungunya and typhus prevention by vector avoidance, food and water safety, and travel vaccines: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Infectious diseases (travel medicine) consultation in two weeks to establish the cause of the recurrent fevers, advise on antirelapse treatment, and plan pre-travel care for the deployment. Guideline: Treatment of Uncomplicated Malaria (clinical guidance) (2026); The practice of travel medicine: guidelines by the Infectious Diseases Society of America (Hill DR, et al. Clin Infect Dis 2006;43(12):1499-1539) (2006) [S]</item><item>Malaria testing between attacks: thick and thin blood smears, rapid antigen test, and Plasmodium species PCR sent to the reference laboratory; quantitative G6PD activity before any primaquine; blood count, kidney and liver tests. Guideline: Treatment of Uncomplicated Malaria (clinical guidance) (2026) [S]</item><item>Fever action plan: a blood smear the same day for any fever, at home, at sea or after travel; carry a card stating his malaria history. Guideline: Treatment of Uncomplicated Malaria (clinical guidance) (2026); CDC Yellow Book: Health Information for International Travel, 2026 edition. Malaria (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to infectious diseases (travel medicine), Jean-Baptiste Okonkwo-Hale, MD, ordered 2026-02-17 [S]</item></list></text>

